  "Question": "Is \\(x^2-1=(x+1)(x-1)\\) a factorization?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "No, because this is polynomial multiplication.",
    "B": "No, because the two sides of the equation are not equal.",
    "C": "Yes, because the polynomial has been rewritten as a product of polynomial expressions.",
    "D": "No, because the right-hand side has not been rewritten as a single polynomial."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Factorization means rewriting a polynomial as a product of polynomial expressions. The right-hand side is precisely in the form of a product of polynomial expressions.",
